# Narrator: Khazan's undercroft under Van Richten's Tower (The Name Over the Door, docs/story/side_quests.md;
# docs/voice/narrator.md). Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ enter:khazan_undercroft
| The stair under the hearth goes down past the level of the lake. The walls sweat cold water. Every step down, the silence gets thicker, like the inside of a library nobody has opened in a long time.
| [flag.khazan_destroyed] The undercroft is only a cellar now: cold, wet, full of old books. Nothing turns a page.
cooldown 30

~ enter:undercroft_stair
| The steps are worn in the middle into shallow bowls, by one pair of feet going up and down them for a very long time, and then by none.
once

~ enter:hall_of_names
| A long low hall with shelves floor to ceiling, and every shelf full. The books have no titles on their spines. There's a smell of old paper and cold water, and under it, something like breath.
once

~ enter:drowned_crypt
| The lake has got in here. Black water stands in the far half of the crypt, perfectly still, and the stone coffins at its edge are wet to the lid.
once

~ enter:khazan_study
| A study, warm with candles that give no heat, crowded with reading tables and books. At the far end, on a step, a high-backed chair.
once

~ examine:undercroft_glyphs
| Letters cut into every step, small, one word to a step, all the way down. The same word. You don't need to read it to know what it says.

~ examine:names_shelves
| You take down a book. Names, one to a line, page after page, in a small neat hand, with a date beside each in a reckoning nobody uses any more. You put it back. It seems to settle, the way a cat does.

~ examine:names_wall
| Names scratched into the wall at shoulder height, by different hands, in different years. Some are prayers. One is a list of a family. The last one just says HELP, and then a name, and stops.

~ examine:names_lectern
| An open book on a lectern. Every name on the open pages has been crossed out in red ink, carefully, with a ruler. At the bottom: "Read. Kept."

~ examine:names_table
| Books open on a table, each at a different page, as if someone had been reading them all at once and got up in the middle.

~ examine:crypt_coffin
| A stone coffin with no name on it. That's the only one down here without a name, and it's the only one with nobody in it.

~ examine:crypt_drip
| The lake comes through the ceiling in a slow drip, and the drip has worn a hole in the floor as round as a bowl. The water is so cold it smokes.

~ search:crypt_bracers
| In the silt at the water's edge, a forearm of bone still wearing a pair of bracers, the leather gone to nothing and the plates still bright. An apprentice's, from the cut of them, who came down to read and stayed.

~ check:investigation:crypt_bracers:failure
| Silt, and bones, and the cold.

~ examine:khazan_circle
| A circle drawn on the floor in something that was silver once, with nothing in the middle of it. When you step near, the candles lean away.

~ examine:khazan_mobile
| A brass orrery, the size of a cartwheel, of a sky that isn't this one: more moons, and one star that's been taken out and its arm left empty.
